WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.735
-It is the end of the week,
and that's usually

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.070
when I catch up with some
personal stuff.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.105
You know, I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.041
and, of course, I send out
thank-you notes.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.875
Well, I was running a bit behind
today, so I thought,

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:11.577
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd just like to write out

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:12.878
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.480
Is that --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.382
You guys are the best.

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:18.985
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.386
♪♪

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:21.421
There it is.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:25.424
♪♪

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:27.560
It looks like he's got secrets.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.363
♪♪

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:33.132
Thank you, "Bachelorette"
getting replaced,

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.735
for only being the second most
famous reality TV star

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.570
to lose their job this week.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.607
[ Applause ]

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.912
♪♪

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.714
Thank you, Steve Kornacki
and John King,

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:51.918
for being the McSteamy
and McDreamy of touchscreens.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:57.156
[ Applause ]

00:00:57.156 --> 00:01:00.192
I love everyone's so impressed
with the touchscreen.

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:02.261
My daughter was using
a touchscreen at six months.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:03.329
She was...

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.531
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:06.932
♪♪

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.934
Thank you, red mirage,

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.403
for sounding less like
a political term

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.272
and more like
the 14th Marvel movie

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.007
to get postponed this year.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.141
[ Applause ]

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.177
"Red Mirage."

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:25.718
♪♪
Man, this one's --

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.220
You might want to help me out
on this one.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.555
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.756
Yeah. I get to phone a friend
on this one.

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:32.658
-Okay.
Try it out.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:34.794
-Yeah, just laugh
even if it's not funny.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.830
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.398
-It's pretty good.

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.033
All right, we'll see.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.702
-Wait, right now? Or --
-What?

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.671
Yeah, now.
Well, after I'm done.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.039
-Okay.
-After I'm done with the joke.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.206
-Okay.

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:48.708
[ Laughs ] That was funny.
-Wait till --

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.843
I didn't do it yet, but once
I do it, then you do it.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.111
Okay, here we go.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.646
-Okay.
-Almost.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.181
♪♪

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:58.017
Thank you, Drake's
new Alpine Yodels,

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:01.154
for not going by your
original name, Yeti Turds.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:04.691
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.992
-Wait.

00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:09.896
What?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.331
-What? That was the original
name they went with?

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:15.068
-Ah.
-I don't know, man.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.102
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:18.971
♪♪

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:21.341
Thank you, fancy wine openers,

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:23.142
for making my guests think
that I'm either

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:25.778
a wine connoisseur
or a steampunk alcoholic.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.547
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.120
♪♪

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.855
Thank you, owls,

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.858
for always looking like you just
read Don Jr.'s latest tweet.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.861
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.496
♪♪

00:02:44.496 --> 00:02:46.298
Thank you, election week,

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.401
for hopefully coming
to an end,

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.937
and for letting us all go back
to a calm, relaxing life

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:53.406
of worrying about
a global pandemic.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.108
There you go. Those are
our thank-you notes.

